- appliedSpendingEvidenceFresh / getSettingsHash: confirmed s.SpendingSearch
  (now carrying FloorMonthlyReal) is assigned at line 638, BEFORE
  s.AppliedSpendingEvidence is nil'd and the hash computed (lines
  648-651), and the same post-hash settings object is what gets saved --
  so the extra field cannot cause spurious staleness. Not specifically
  covered by a dedicated new assertion, but TestSpendingApplyKeepsComparison
  Minimum's "current-with-rules"/"searched" runs call
  spendingOptimizerFormData(got, nil) after Apply and get the expected
  values, which would not happen if the hash/settings pairing were broken
  in a way that mattered to this path; separately
  TestSpendingApplySavesSearchPreferences explicitly asserts
  appliedSpendingEvidenceFresh(got) is true post-apply.
- omitempty/0 floor: parseSpendingRequest rejects `n <= 0` for
  floor_monthly_real (required=true), so FloorMonthlyReal can never be a
  legitimately-saved 0 that omitempty would silently drop from JSON. Also
  directly asserted by TestSpendingOptimizerFormMinimumRequiresSavedFloor's
  "no-policy"/"no-floor" cases expecting `"FloorMonthlyReal":null` in the
  JSON-encoded form data.
- Prepare/Cancel flow: grepped every write of `s.SpendingSearch` in
  handlers_spending_optimizer.go -- exactly one, at line 638, inside Apply.
  Prepare is read-only re preferences persistence; nothing writes
  SpendingSearch before Apply.
- Scenario save: SaveWithRevisionIfScenario receives the same `s` that
  carries the new SpendingSearch, same call already exercised by
  TestSpendingApplyKeepsComparisonMinimum via rm.Load()/LoadContextWithRevision
  after Apply, which round-trips through the real storage layer (JSON file),
